2026-11-06T03:01:27.8870784Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8879363Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8880358Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8881099Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8881462Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8881772Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8882308Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8882770Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8883597Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8883945Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8884068Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8884358Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8886241Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8886501Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8886904Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:01:27.8887068Z 
